  "final_message": "I wrote `answer.json` with four functions in `billing/subscriptions.py` that emit `subscription.updated` directly:\n\n- `subscriptions.transition` emits it for every status change except a move to `canceled`, which emits `subscription.canceled` instead.\n- `subscriptions.change_items` emits it after replacing the items.\n- `subscriptions.cancel` emits it when it only schedules cancellation at period end. An immediate cancel goes through `transition` and emits `subscription.canceled`.\n- `subscriptions.reactivate` emits it when it clears a scheduled cancellation.\n\nI didn't run the tests; I found these by grepping and reading the code. The grep for the literal string found no other emitters. Callers such as `pause`, `resume` and the dunning code reach the event only through `transition`, so I left them out.",
